    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nAs far as I know, \ncurrently if we create directory marks in `mini.files` and relaunch nvim after quitting it then all the directory marks get removed automatically. When you have a deeper directory structure marks then marking again those marks could become a hectic/annoying work.  \n\nSo idea is to make all the marks persist in a file inside `shada/data/cache` directory for current pwd, so when we return after exit all marks can be loaded again. \n\nfunctionalities expected in this feature: \nmarking again with same directory with same mark should remove the mark. (echo message mark `a` on `dir` has removed) \nmake all marks persist in a file(.json) most likely in `shada/data/cache`, load it when mini.files is launched for first time.\n\nOr correct me if the functionality already exists, I will withdraw this issue.",
